  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md's real per-field bit tables (0x0300-0x0338), cited by contract ID below -- same disclosed scope/rationale as rtl002_field_map.json's own _source note (extract_registers.py does not currently preserve per-field bit ranges project-wide). EVT_OVERFLOW_COUNT/EVT_POP_ERROR_COUNT are REG-002 access class COUNTER-CLR (read 0x00000000-0xFFFFFFFF; writes only 0x00000000 or 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF emits one clear pulse, every other word is ACCESS_ERROR) -- reggen.py v4 has no dedicated COUNTER-CLR pulse-capture path, so these two fields are mapped with class \"W1C\" here to reuse its existing one-cycle raw-wdata_i pulse-capture logic (identical mechanism, a real one-cycle pulse of whatever was written). dfc_rtl005.sv itself checks the pulse value is exactly 32'hFFFFFFFF before treating it as an accepted clear (0 is naturally a no-op; any other value is neither a legal COUNTER-CLR write nor validated/rejected as ACCESS_ERROR, since RTL-001 has no per-field write-value validation yet -- OPEN_ISSUES.md item 4, a pre-existing gap this does not worsen).",
